Sharp transition: constants c <= 1 reach tan(theta) <= eps; c > 1 fail to converge to the target (the perturbation magnitude exceeds what the accelerated contraction can absorb). The paper's own proven constant c=1/32 is well inside the safe region; the empirical failure boundary (c~1) shows the CONSTANT has analysis slack, but the FUNCTIONAL FORM (linear in gap*eps, i.e. cannot be scaled up by an arbitrary constant) is tight: relaxing it enough (c>1 here) breaks convergence.

